    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0892" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1551b: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)<anchor n="6a"
                        xml:id="d664-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-03T16:00:00-05:00">October 3, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I appreciate the full and complete information you are sending and I know that
                    you will keep us closely informed of the attitude of the <pb facs="0893" n="791"
                        xml:id="pg791"/> British Government toward events as they develop. In order
                    that I may be in a position, however, to advise the President in connection with
                    the requirement that an embargo on shipment of arms, ammunition and implements
                    of war be declared “upon the outbreak or during the progress of war between or
                    among two or more foreign states,” I am particularly anxious to receive any
                    information which would have a bearing upon the President’s decision as to
                    whether war has broken out or is in progress.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d664-f1" n="6a" type="source" xml:id="d664-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, October 3, to the
                    Ambassadors in France and Italy, and to the Consul at Geneva; also a similar
                    instruction on the same date to the Chargé in Ethiopia as telegram No. 63.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
